-\paragraph{Efficiency.} Under its selected attack, R3's gross efficiency falls from \site{ch_eff_1} at $p = \const{0.01}$ to \site{ch_eff_5} at \const{0.05} (\site{ch_eff_5d} with the doubled searches); C$^*$'s is \site{ch_eff_c5} at \const{0.05} and changes little across the rates (Table~\ref{tab:ph-churn-audit}); at \const{0.05} B3's is \site{ch_eff_b5} with the frozen and \site{ch_eff_b5d} with the doubled searches, and across the rates it shows no trend in $p$, only changes of the selected attack on single markets. On \site{ch_eff_minm} at $p = \const{0.05}$, R3's efficiency under attack is \site{ch_eff_min}, below the registered threshold of \const{0.90}; this is an exploratory point estimate, not a registered failure. The registered efficiency condition is a no-churn result.
