    version (only doubled B3 minus R3 at p = 0.05 excludes zero); the text
    says the churn reversals are measured on six markets and not
    established beyond them. Crossings stated per search version; C*
    unresolved at 0.01 and 0.02, negative on all six markets at 0.03 under
    both versions; no 'holds its own only without churn'. B3 gap rises at
    0.01 before it falls. Mechanism values labelled frozen, doubled range
    added. C* efficiency 'changes little'; B3 range limited to p = 0.05.
    Failed-search note beside -0.052 in the conclusion. Run A: fresh5
    dominates but does not set the sign; the four rows, C* minus runner-up
    and the runner-up flags. churn_paper.py: --summary requires --runnerup,
    t table with a stale check; tests first (summary_r6_red.log,
    t_table_red.log); 10 tests pass; gate ok. Astra round-2 output added.
    
